  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `ShareTokenUpgradeable` contract states in its natspec that it is fully EIP 7575 compliant as the share token of the multi-asset vault system but this is not the case. The EIP 7575 specification declares:\n> The share contract SHOULD implement the ERC-165 supportsInterface function. The share token MUST return the constant value true if 0xf815c03d is passed through the interfaceID argument.\n\nAs `ShareTokenUpgradeable` does implement the supportsInterface function, it must return true for the constant value `0xf815c03d` passed in as the interfaceID, but it returns false instead. This would lead to integration errors with external systems that depend on this feature.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nModify the supportsInterface function to return the missing signature",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add the below test to `AuditReproduction.t.sol`:\nfunction testNonCompliant() public {\n        bool isValid = mainShareToken.supportsInterface(0xf815c03d);\n        assert(isValid == false);\n    }",
